# HR AI Platform — environment variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is a quick-reference index. The client and server each read
# their own .env file, which is the source of truth:
#   client/.env  (copy from client/.env.example)
#   server/.env  (copy from server/.env.example)
#
# For the full list with descriptions of what each variable does and
# which are required vs. optional, see those two files directly — this
# one only lists the names. See README.md's "Deployment" section for
# what to enter on Render (server) and Netlify (client) in production.

# ===== client/.env =====
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_API_URL=

# ===== server/.env =====
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
CLIENT_ORIGIN=
PORT=
NODE_ENV=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=
INTEGRATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
SUPABASE_JWKS_JSON=
ESCALATION_TEST_MODE=
